[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mWait — I need to reconsider [38;5;10malgorithm2[0m. The C code processes columns in chunks of 8 and within each chunk, the inner k loop is unrolled by 8. The SIMD operations multiply 8 elements at a time and accumulate into [38;5;10mc[i][k][0m. But the k loop also increments by 8 inside the loop body (k++ appears 7 times after the initial k). So the effective behavior is: for each block of 8 columns j..j+8, for each k in steps of 8, compute the dot product of [38;5;10ma[i][j..j+8][0m with [38;5;10mb[k..k+8][j..j+8][0m and add to [38;5;10mc[i][k..k+8][0m.[0m[0m
