Actually, looking more carefully at the SIMD code: [38;5;10mm_a[0m is loaded once per j-block as [38;5;10ma[i][j..j+8][0m. Then for each k (stepping by 8), it loads [38;5;10mb[k][j..j+8][0m, multiplies element-wise with [38;5;10mm_a[0m, and sums all 8 products into [38;5;10mc[i][k][0m. This is computing partial dot products of row i of a with row k of b (where b is the transpose of bb). Summing across all j-blocks gives the full dot product.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
So the net result is indeed [38;5;10mc[i][k] = sum_j(a[i][j] * b[k][j])[0m = [38;5;10msum_j(a[i][j] * bb[j][k])[0m which is standard matrix multiplication. My implementation is correct.[0m[0m
